 in the advent of the Industrial Revolution, up to the Saturn V rocket (1967). While by no means a comprehensive list, these landmarks represent what the mechanical engineering profession considers to be both unusual and significant achievements through the eyes of ASME International (the American Society of Mechanical Engineers).\n\nAs a worldwide engineering society focused on technical, educational, and research issues, ASME International conducts one of the world's largest technical publishing operations, holds some thirty technical conferences and two hundred professional development courses each year, and sets many industrial and manufacturing standards. "
